			"id": "agent-analysis-uiability-backup-restore-state-recovery",
			"interpretation": "Independently buildable HarmonyOS Stage-model sample demonstrating UIAbility backup-and-restore after abnormal exit. Responsibility: keep the implementation files (EntryAbility.ets, pages/Index.ets), the backup extension (EntryBackupAbility.ets), module wiring (module.json5), backup_config.json, and the ohosTest Oracle (Ability.test.ets) coherent as one snippet. Boundary: runtime code is the two .ets files under entry/src/main/ets; the Oracle surface is the ohosTest suite under entry/src/ohosTest/ets/test; the 7-day retention, 200KB Want cap, and no-reboot-restore claims live only in README_zh.md. Relations: EntryAbility imports @kit.AbilityKit, @kit.ArkUI, @kit.PerformanceAnalysisKit; EntryBackupAbility imports @kit.CoreFileKit; the test imports @ohos/hypium and @kit.TestKit; module.json5 sets mainElement/srcEntry EntryAbility and registers a backup extensionAbilities entry with $profile:backup_config (allowToBackupRestore:true). Behavior contract: onCreate calls setRestoreEnabled(true) in try/catch and reads want.parameters['myData'] into an unused local; onSaveState writes wantParam['myData']='my1234567' and returns ALL_AGREE; Index toggles @State message from 'Hello World' to 'Welcome' on click. Oracle: UIAbility_Recover_01 starts EntryAbility via abilityDelegator, delays 1000ms, asserts the top ability is 'EntryAbility'. Keep srcEntry/mainElement names, the backup flag, and the [Start]/[End]/[StartExclude]/[EndExclude] doc-snippet markers consistent when refactoring.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["The end-to-end restore path is not proved in code: the value read from want.parameters['myData'] in onCreate is stored in an unused local, and Index.ets holds only a static 'Hello World'/'Welcome' toggle with no logic to rebuild page state from restored data, so the README's claim that page stack and onSaveState data are recovered is not demonstrated by this checkout.","No build, deploy, emulator, or device execution was performed; the README's stated constraints (RK3568, DevEco Studio version, API level) and its backup-retention claims are unverified doc statements.","The ohosTest entry only asserts that a cold startAbility launch reaches the top; it does not exercise setRestoreEnabled, onSaveState, kill-and-relaunch recovery, or the restored Want parameter, so the sample's recovery behavior has no executable Oracle coverage in this checkout.","Retention claims in README_zh.md (7-day backup storage, 200KB Want serialization limit, no restore across device reboot) are platform behaviors asserted by documentation only; nothing in the checked-in files proves them.","module.json5, backup_config.json, EntryBackupAbility.ets, and the remaining test/list files are pinned from the prior verified fact at the same HEAD revision (blob OIDs re-checked via git rev-parse); only the three refreshed evidence blobs were re-derived this round.","'myData' appears only in EntryAbility.ets; no other tracked file under Ability/UIAbilityRecover references the restored key, so any consumer must be introduced within these files."],
